					<div id="mw-content-text" class="mw-body-content"><div class="mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output" lang="en" dir="ltr" data-mw-parsoid-version="0.24.0.0-alpha27" data-mw-html-version="2.8.0"><section data-mw-section-id="0" id="mwAQ"><div class="shortdescription nomobile noexcerpt noprint searchaux" style="display:none" about="#mwt1" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwAg" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Short description","href":"./Template:Short_description"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"List of companies in the S&amp;P 500"}},"i":0}}]}'>List of companies in the S&amp;P 500</div><span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_with_short_description"/><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Short_description_is_different_from_Wikidata"/></span>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt2" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwAw" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"for","href":"./Template:For"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"a list of previous components of the index"},"2":{"wt":"Historical components of the S&amp;P 500"}},"i":0}}]}'><style data-mw-deduplicate="TemplateStyles:r1368532237" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" about="#mwt3" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'>.mw-parser-output .hatnote{font-style:italic}.mw-parser-output div.hatnote{padding-left:1.6em;margin-bottom:0.5em}.mw-parser-output .hatnote i{font-style:normal}.mw-parser-output .hatnote+.mw-empty-elt+.hatnote{margin-top:-0.5em}@media print{body.ns-0 .mw-parser-output .hatnote{display:none!important}}</style></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt2" id="mwBA">For a list of previous components of the index, see <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Historical_components_of_the_S&amp;P_500" title="Historical components of the S&amp;P 500">Historical components of the S&amp;P 500</a>.</div>
<p class="mw-empty-elt" id="mwBQ"><span typeof="mw:Nowiki mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt4" id="mwBg" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Use American English","href":"./Template:Use_American_English"},"params":{"date":{"wt":"August 2026"}},"i":0}}]}'></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Use_American_English_from_August_2026" about="#mwt4"/><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:All_Wikipedia_articles_written_in_American_English" about="#mwt4" id="mwBw"/>
<span typeof="mw:Nowiki mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt5" id="mwCA" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Use mdy dates","href":"./Template:Use_mdy_dates"},"params":{"date":{"wt":"August 2026"}},"i":0}}]}'></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Use_mdy_dates_from_August_2026" about="#mwt5" id="mwCQ"/></p>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwCg"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:S&amp;P_500_Headquarters.svg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwCw"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:S&amp;P_500_Headquarters.svg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/S%26P_500_Headquarters.svg/250px-S%26P_500_Headquarters.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/S%26P_500_Headquarters.svg/500px-S%26P_500_Headquarters.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="10207" data-file-height="5490" data-file-type="drawing" height="134" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwDA"/></a><figcaption id="mwDQ">Locations of headquarters of the components of the S&amp;P 500</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwDg">The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/S&amp;P_500" title="S&amp;P 500" id="mwDw">S&amp;P 500</a> is a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stock_market_index" title="Stock market index" id="mwEA">stock market index</a> maintained by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/S&amp;P_Dow_Jones_Indices" title="S&amp;P Dow Jones Indices" id="mwEQ">S&amp;P Dow Jones Indices</a>. It comprises 503 <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Common_stock" title="Common stock" id="mwEg">common stocks</a> which are issued by 500 companies with large <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Market_capitalization" title="Market capitalization" id="mwEw">market capitalizations</a>, including two share classes of stock from three of its component companies: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alphabet_Inc." title="Alphabet Inc." id="mwFA">Alphabet</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fox_Corporation" title="Fox Corporation" id="mwFQ">Fox Corporation</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/News_Corp" title="News Corp" id="mwFg">News Corp</a>. The index includes about 80% of the American stock market by capitalization. It is weighted by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Capitalization-weighted_index#Free-float_weighting" title="Capitalization-weighted index" id="mwFw">free-float</a> market capitalization.<sup about="#mwt8" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Methodology_1-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Methodology"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Methodology-1"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Methodology-1" id="mwGA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwGQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwGg">[</span>1<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwGw">]</span></span></a></sup> An updated weighting of each component is available <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.ssga.com/us/en/intermediary/etfs/state-street-spdr-sp-500-etf-trust-spy" class="external text" id="mwHA">online</a>.</p>
<p id="mwHQ">
<!--EDITORS PLEASE TAKE NOTE:

 If you are updating the following table due to a change which occurred in the components of the S&#x26;P 500 please consider the following.

 1. S&#x26;P rarely adds or removes a stock in isolation, it's almost always "AAA replaced BBB". If this is the case, please do not simply add or remove a component; Rather, make sure you record both parts of the change.

 2. If you record a change, please also make an entry in the article Historical components of the S&#x26;P 500. Keeping these two tables in sync should make it much easier for editors to keep track of which changes have/haven't been entered.

 3. Most of the dates in the "Date added" column agree with the date in the Standard &#x26; Poors spreadsheet that first included the new company, but others list the last day of trading when the replaced company was considered part of the index (i.e., the prior business day). Interested parties are invited to participate in the discussion near the end of the "talk" page in the section titled "Dates of changes for newly added S&#x26;P 500 components".

Thanks -->
<br id="mwHg"/></p>
